{"id":9170,"date":"2020-12-07T00:00:00","date_gmt":"2020-12-07T07:00:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.rethinkfirst.com\/resources\/teaching-multiply-controlled-intraverbal-behavior-webinar\/"},"modified":"2024-10-03T17:32:58","modified_gmt":"2024-10-03T21:32:58","slug":"teaching-multiply-controlled-intraverbal-behavior-webinar","status":"publish","type":"resources","link":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/resources\/teaching-multiply-controlled-intraverbal-behavior-webinar\/","title":{"rendered":"Teaching Multiply Controlled Intraverbal Behavior"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>The analysis of multiple control in the intraverbal relation is critical for moving individuals with autism and related language delays towards naturalistic conversational repertoires.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>One area in this analysis is \u201cverbal conditional discriminations,\u201d when multiple verbal stimuli evoke a verbal response, such as answering &#8220;parrot&#8221; when asked, &#8220;What&#8217;s an animal that&#8217;s red?&#8221;.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>A second area is answering questions about visual stimuli, such as answering &#8220;green&#8221; when shown a picture of a frog and asked, &#8220;What color?&#8221;<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The presenter will provide definitions, examples, studies, and analyses on these topics.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong><a href=\"\/wp-content\/uploads\/2022\/06\/Multiply-Controlled-Intraverbals-Rethink-Webinar-notes-1.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Download Multiply Controlled Intraverbals &#8211; Rethink Webinar &#8211; Notes <i class=\"fa fa-download\"><\/i><\/a><\/strong><\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":19,"featured_media":15019,"template":"","meta":{"_seopress_robots_primary_cat":"","_seopress_titles_title":"Webinar: Teaching Multiply Controlled Intraverbal Behavior","_seopress_titles_desc":"Multiple control analysis in intraverbal relation is critical to move autism & related language delays individuals to naturalistic conversation repertoires.","_seopress_robots_index":"","om_disable_all_campaigns":false,"_links_to":"","_links_to_target":""},"audience":[70],"resource-type":[72],"resource-topic":[97,329,86],"resource-tag":[336,269,156],"class_list":["post-9170","resources","type-resources","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","audience-providers","resource-type-webinar","resource-topic-autism","resource-topic-behavior","resource-topic-tips-tools-tech","resource-tag-asd","resource-tag-communication","resource-tag-teacher"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resources\/9170","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resources"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/resources"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/19"}],"version-history":[{"count":0,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resources\/9170\/revisions"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/15019"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=9170"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"audience","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/audience?post=9170"},{"taxonomy":"resource-type","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resource-type?post=9170"},{"taxonomy":"resource-topic","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resource-topic?post=9170"},{"taxonomy":"resource-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/www.rethinkbehavioralhealth.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/resource-tag?post=9170"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}